cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Shadow Hunter: Label-Free Zone Selection for Shadow-Based
  Building Height Estimation
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - name: Shadow Hunter contributors
repository-code: https://github.com/Jarvis-Mi/shadowhunter
url: https://github.com/Jarvis-Mi/shadowhunter
abstract: >-
  Shadow Hunter estimates building height from free satellite imagery in two
  stages. A deep reinforcement-learning agent pans and rescales a window over a
  tile until it isolates a single, unoccluded, unclipped building shadow,
  guided only by label-free proxy rewards computed from the crop and the sun
  angle in the image metadata. A physics-anchored convolutional network then
  reads that crop and predicts a residual around the analytic estimate
  h = L tan(theta), together with a calibrated uncertainty. Because the zone
  selector needs no ground-truth heights, the method transfers to cities where
  no height labels exist.
keywords:
  - remote-sensing
  - reinforcement-learning
  - computer-vision
  - building-height
  - shadow
  - sentinel-2
  - spacenet
  - label-free
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-08-29'
